.TH TC 8 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tc \- traffic control (unsupported)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tc
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Substrate has no queueing-discipline or traffic-control subsystem.
.B tc
is a placeholder that ignores all arguments, prints
.RS
.B tc: traffic control is not supported on this system
.RE
on standard error and exits unsuccessfully, so that scripts do not
mistake it for having installed a rule.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B tc
always exits with status
.BR 1 .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tcp (7),
.BR substrate (7)
